Third-party components
======================

OpenTabletDriver (LGPL-3.0)
  https://github.com/OpenTabletDriver/OpenTabletDriver
  Used as the tablet driver: OpenTabletArtist bundles and talks to the OTD
  daemon and links its libraries (vendored, with patches, in
  external/OpenTabletDriver). Licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0, which
  is compatible with this program's GPL-3.0 license.

HidSharpCore 1.3.0 (Apache-2.0)
  https://github.com/OpenTabletDriver/HidSharpCore (commit bca4aee)
  The HID library of the OpenTabletDriver daemon. Vendored in external/HidSharpCore
  and modified for issue #118 (macOS devices told apart by registry entry ID); the
  changes are listed in external/HidSharpCore/VENDORED.md. Its NOTICE reads:
    HIDSharp
    Copyright 2010-2019 James F. Bellinger <http://www.zer7.com/software/hidsharp>
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (external/HidSharpCore/LICENSE),
  which is compatible with this program's GPL-3.0 license.

VoiDPlugins — "Windows Ink" output-mode plugin (GPL-3.0)   [planned — see #319]
  https://github.com/Kuuuube/VoiDPlugins
  OpenTabletArtist plans to bundle the "Windows Ink" output-mode plugin from
  VoiDPlugins so it is available without a separate download (issue #319). When
  the plugin binary is bundled, the exact upstream release/commit it was built
  from will be recorded alongside it so the corresponding source is always
  available, as required by the GPL. VoiDPlugins is licensed under GPL-3.0.

Ideas from MockTab (Cyzor), GPL-3: full settings backup and restore, the one-click diagnostic file,
and the running-process tablet-driver conflict check (process names from MockTab's ConflictProcessMatcher).
Reimplemented in C#; no MockTab code is copied. https://github.com/Cyzor/tablet-driver
